{"id":"h09t4","name":"Group Seat Assignment","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["rows","requests"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A plane has <code>rows</code> rows numbered from 1. Each row has six seats: <code>A B C</code>, the aisle, then <code>D E F</code>. Seats are written like <code>12C</code>. All seats are free at the start. Process <code>requests</code> in order:</p>\n<ul><li><code>\"BOOK id k\"</code> (<code>k</code> is 1, 2 or 3): a group of <code>k</code> passengers who must sit side by side on the same side of the aisle in the same row. The group gets the first free option in this order: row 1 first, then row 2, and so on; inside a row, the options are tried in this order:\n<ul><li><code>k = 1</code>: <code>A</code>, <code>F</code>, <code>C</code>, <code>D</code>, <code>B</code>, <code>E</code> (window, then aisle, then middle);</li>\n<li><code>k = 2</code>: <code>AB</code>, <code>EF</code>, <code>BC</code>, <code>DE</code>;</li>\n<li><code>k = 3</code>: <code>ABC</code>, <code>DEF</code>.</li></ul>\nReturn <code>\"id:seats\"</code> with the seats joined by <code>\",\"</code> in letter order (for example <code>\"7:3E,3F\"</code>), or <code>\"id:FULL\"</code> if no option is free (nothing is booked). A booking id that already has seats is refused with <code>\"id:DUPLICATE\"</code>.</li>\n<li><code>\"CANCEL id\"</code>: frees all the seats of the booking. Return <code>\"id:CANCELLED\"</code>, or <code>\"id:UNKNOWN\"</code> if the id has no seats (never booked, refused or already cancelled). A cancelled id can be booked again later.</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to return one string per request.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>rows = 2, requests = [\"BOOK g1 3\", \"BOOK g2 2\", \"BOOK g3 1\", \"BOOK g4 2\", \"BOOK g5 3\", \"CANCEL g1\", \"BOOK g6 2\", \"BOOK g2 1\", \"CANCEL g9\", \"BOOK g7 1\", \"BOOK g8 1\", \"BOOK g9 3\"]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[\"g1:1A,1B,1C\", \"g2:1E,1F\", \"g3:1D\", \"g4:2A,2B\", \"g5:2D,2E,2F\", \"g1:CANCELLED\", \"g6:1A,1B\", \"g2:DUPLICATE\", \"g9:UNKNOWN\", \"g7:1C\", \"g8:2C\", \"g9:FULL\"]</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> integer rows<br><b>[input]</b> array.string requests<br><b>[output]</b> array.string</div>","starter":"def solution(rows, requests):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["règles de préférence","allée","annulations","réservation qui échoue","ordre de recherche"],"minutes":30,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solution(rows, requests)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Ici, la valeur attendue est une liste : compare ce que tu renvoies à « Expected return value » dans les résultats.</li><li>La comparaison est exacte (même type, mêmes valeurs, même ordre dans une liste), sauf les nombres décimaux, comparés à 0,000001 près.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 9 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"rows":2,"requests":["BOOK g1 3","BOOK g2 2","BOOK g3 1","BOOK g4 2","BOOK g5 3","CANCEL g1","BOOK g6 2","BOOK g2 1","CANCEL g9","BOOK g7 1","BOOK g8 1","BOOK g9 3"]},"expected":{"value":["g1:1A,1B,1C","g2:1E,1F","g3:1D","g4:2A,2B","g5:2D,2E,2F","g1:CANCELLED","g6:1A,1B","g2:DUPLICATE","g9:UNKNOWN","g7:1C","g8:2C","g9:FULL"]}},{"input":{"rows":1,"requests":["BOOK a 1","BOOK b 1","BOOK c 1","BOOK d 2","CANCEL a","CANCEL a","BOOK a 2","BOOK e 1","BOOK f 1"]},"expected":{"value":["a:1A","b:1F","c:1C","d:1D,1E","a:CANCELLED","a:UNKNOWN","a:1A,1B","e:FULL","f:FULL"]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}